Wait — `env.setMtime` on a file written via `writeFile` — the memory fs `writeFile` stamps real wall clock; setMtime overrides. The store's clock: my sweep uses `_clock()` vs the file's mtime — setMtime makes it deterministic. Good — same pattern as the existing TTL test.

One subtlety: MemoryExecutionEnv.listDir on `.fah/trajectories` — when only s1 exists... in test 1 the root exists. For the "no-op" case (nothing written at all): listDir('.fah/trajectories') returns Err(notFound) → valueOrNull null → 0 iterations → 0. 

