Hmm wait — where to call sweepOncePerBoot? Inside `write` at the top, or have hosts call it? If inside `write`, hosts don't change at all. Let me put it at the top of `write`:

```dart
 Future<TrajectoryRequestSpill?> write({...}) async {
  if (!_bootSwept) {
    _bootSwept = true;
    await sweepExpiredEverywhere();
  }
  ...
``

Clean; both hosts inherit it. And `sweepExpiredEverywhere` public for tests/future hosts.

```dart
 /// Deletes every blob past [ttlDays] in EVERY session's request dir
 /// under `.fah/trajectories/` — the disk-footprint tail survives the
 /// per-session rotation otherwise (ended sessions never write again).
 /// Returns the deleted count; best-effort (listing failures skip that
 /// dir, removal failures are swallowed).
 Future<int> sweepExpiredEverywhere() async {
  var deleted = 0;
  final root = await _env.listDir('.fah/trajectories');
  for (final entry in root.valueOrNull ?? const <FileInfo>[]) {
    if (entry.kind != FileKind.directory) continue;
    deleted += await _sweepExpiredIn(
      '${'.fah/trajectories'}/${entry.name}/requests',
    );
  }
  return deleted;
 }

 Future<int> _sweepExpiredIn(String dir) async {
  final listing = await _env.listDir(dir);
  final files = listing.valueOrNull;
  if (files == null || files.isEmpty) return 0;
  final now = _clock();
  final ttl = Duration(days: ttlDays);
  var deleted = 0;
  for (final file in files) {
    final expired =
        now.difference(DateTime.fromMillisecondsSinceEpoch(file.mtimeMs)) >
        ttl;
    if (!expired) continue;
    final removed = await _env.remove(file.path, force: true);
    if (removed.isOk) deleted++;
  }
  return deleted;
 }
``

Check FileKind is exported from execution_env.dart (the test imports flutter_agent_harness.dart — FileKind is exported? execution_env.dart is exported via the package barrel presumably). For lib-internal use it doesn't matter.

Wait — should the boot sweep apply to `enforceBudget`'s newest-kept semantics? No — separate semantics, documented.

Edge: the live session's OWN dir is swept too — a fresh blob survives (not expired). Good.

Also note: `trajectoryRequestBlobDir` builds `.fah/trajectories/${sid ?? 'sessionless'}/requests`. My sweep derives `.fah/trajectories/<name>/requests` for every dir entry — includes sessionless. Consistent.

